{"type": "say", "text": "Hi everyone! So, as you all know, I'm in charge of organizing the food and the practical serving plan for Aunt June's retirement brunch this Sunday at the Oak Street community hall. We've got about twenty-five guests expected to eat around 12:30, and the hall has a kitchen and folding tables we can use. One important constraint: we need to get the tables arranged before noon because there's another event in the room that afternoon. I'd love to hear your thoughts on what kind of food we should serve and any other practical considerations we should plan around. What do you all think?"}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Hey Evan, yeah, you did mention the celiac thing to me a while back — sorry I didn't pass it along sooner. Nora, we definitely need to factor that in. I actually have something to share about the menu too, but let me get to that in a moment. As for the tables, since they need to be set up before noon and we're eating at 12:30, maybe a couple of us could arrive by 11:00 or so to get the layout done and have the kitchen prepped?"}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "Hi everyone, I need to share something important about the food plan. My six-year-old son has a severe sesame allergy, so the brunch food must contain absolutely no sesame, and I'd really need the dishes to have ingredient labels so I can make sure everything is safe for him. I told Marcus about this a while back but hadn't brought it up with the rest of you yet — I'm sorry about the timing. Nora, can we please factor this into the food and serving plan along with Evan's celiac needs?"}
```

```json
{
  "type": "say",
  "text": "Thank you all for bringing these things forward — they're all important and I'm glad we're getting them on the table now. Let me recap what I'm working with so far: Evan needs everything gluten-free with separate serving utensils to prevent cross-contamination. Tessa needs the entire menu sesame-free with ingredient labels on each dish for her son's safety. Marcus, thanks for flagging the broken fridge — that's critical since we're eating at 12:30. So all perishable food will need to come in insulated coolers, arriving no later than 12:00. Lila, you mentioned you had something to share about the menu — I'd like to hear that before I start finalizing decisions. And the 11:00 arrival idea for table setup and kitchen prep sounds smart given the before-noon constraint. Lila, what did you want to share about the menu?"
}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks for recapping all of that, Nora — I appreciate you taking the celiac needs seriously. The separate serving utensils are just as important as the gluten-free ingredients, so I'd suggest we plan for dedicated utensils per dish with clear labels so everyone can tell which is which. That might actually pair well with Tessa's ingredient label idea — we could label each dish with both its ingredients and its serving utensil so it covers both the sesame allergy and the cross-contamination concern. I'll hold off on further suggestions until we hear what Lila has to share about the menu, since that might change things."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Lila, that's a great find — Aunt June's lentil pie as the centerpiece makes perfect sense for her retirement celebration. From a practical standpoint, since the fridge is broken, we'll definitely need to transport it in an insulated cooler and have it arrive by 12:00. One thing to check: does the recipe card happen to list the ingredients? That would help us verify it's gluten-free for Evan and sesame-free for Tessa's son, and if it's not already gluten-free, we could look into whether a lentil pie can be adapted with a gluten-free crust or alternative. Either way, I'm happy to help coordinate the cooler logistics for the lentil pie and any other perishable sides."}
```

```json
{
  "type": "say",
  "text": "Great question, Tessa — and Marcus, you're right to flag that too. Lila, before I can finalize anything, I really need to see what's on that recipe card. Could you share the full ingredient list with us now, or at least confirm whether the lentil pie recipe contains any wheat/flour (for Evan's celiac needs) or any sesame products like sesame oil, sesame seeds, or tahini (for Tessa's son)? If the recipe does include either, we'll need to know so we can figure out whether it can be safely adapted or whether we need a backup plan. This is the last piece I need before I can make my final decisions on the menu and serving plan."
}
