```json
{
  "type": "say",
  "text": "Okay, I think I have enough to make final decisions. Here's what I'm settling on: Lila, I appreciate you finding the recipe card, but I agree with Marcus and Tessa — waiting until Sunday to verify ingredients is too risky given Evan's celiac disease and Tessa's son's severe sesame allergy. So here's my plan: Aunt June's lentil pie will be the main dish IF Lila can confirm the full ingredient list is both gluten-free and sesame-free within the next two days. As a contingency, I'm also going to plan a safe backup main dish now — a gluten-free, sesame-free quiche or frittata — so we're not scrambling if the lentil pie recipe can't be verified or adapted. Either way, the menu will be fully gluten-free and sesame-free. Every dish will have ingredient labels and dedicated, labeled serving utensils. All perishable food arrives in insulated coolers by 12:00 since the fridge is broken. Setup crew arrives at 11:00 for tables and kitchen prep. Evan brings label cards and markers; Tessa brings pre-made ingredient label cards; Marcus handles cooler logistics. Lila, please track down that full recipe ASAP — if you can't confirm it by Friday, we go with the backup. Does everyone agree with this plan?"
}
